  "creation": {
    "name": "Caerwyn",
    "premise": "Two days before the Centennial Assembly in Caerwyn, the player character is riding the last miles of the King's Road into the city for the Assembly, on a carter's farm cart piled with cushions for the Assembly's seats, beside the old carter, Barnaby Fitch, and his granddaughter Tansy, who offered them a lift at the last inn. The game begins on the cart at the crossroads nine miles out, late in the afternoon. They're coming to Caerwyn on their own account: they've never met the King, nobody at court has asked anything of them, and none of the story's named people know them yet. What happens on the road brings them to the King that evening, and by the morning of the eve he'll have asked them to look into a death; none of that has happened yet.",
