    "begins": "It ends where the game begins: this afternoon, on the last miles of the King's Road, riding into Caerwyn on a carter's cart of cushions for the Assembly. Say why they're going to Caerwyn for the Assembly (their reasons are their own: work, a debt, a sight to see, somebody to find), not how anything goes. They've never met the King or anyone at court, and nobody has asked anything of them: nothing in their past is part of the story to come."
